From 87cc0d01c70d78cd438e409a50d91efb81c2a38c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:41:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] drm/amdgpu, drm/radeon: Prefer exact bus match for VFCT
 images

The VFCT soft filter added in commits db7e8108809a and 4059e2f02c8a
takes the first VFCT image whose vendor, device, slot and function
match, even when a later image also matches the bus number.  On
systems with several identical GPUs every GPU then gets the first GPU's
image.  This came up during review of the soft filter ("how they would
interplay with a system with multiple of the same GPU") and Alex pointed
out that some Apple systems do exactly that.  The Mac Pro 6,1 is one:

  02:00.0 1002:6798 113-C3861XA-028
  06:00.0 1002:6798 113-C3861XB-028

These patches scan the whole table and prefer the image with an exact bus
match, falling back to the first identity match only when no bus number
matches, so the pci=realloc case the soft filter was added for still
works.

The fallback is still ambiguous when the buses of several identical GPUs
are renumbered: they all get the first image, as they do today.  Refusing
the VFCT image in that case would be stricter, but it could leave a GPU
with no VBIOS at all, so these patches leave that behaviour alone.

Testing, on Mac Pro 6,1s (2x FirePro D700, Apple VFCT above):

- Replayed the machine's VFCT through amdgpu_acpi_vfct_bios() and
  radeon_acpi_vfct_bios() compiled in userspace, before and after this
  series on amd-staging-drm-next.  Before, the GPU at 06:00.0 gets
  113-C3861XA-028; after, it gets 113-C3861XB-028.  An exact-bus
  single-GPU table, a renumbered single-GPU table, a table with both
  buses renumbered and a non-matching device ID behave as before.
- amdgpu: the same change backported to 6.12.111, 7.2.9 and 7.3-rc7.
  On 7.3-rc7 six Mac Pros report 113-C3861XA-028 for 02:00.0 and
  113-C3861XB-028 for 06:00.0 in vbios_version, with no bus mismatch
  notice.
- radeon: only the 6.12.111 backport was booted, once, on one Mac Pro;
  both GPUs initialized with no VFCT warning or bus mismatch notice.
  radeon doesn't log which VBIOS source it used.
- Both files build with W=1, with and without CONFIG_ACPI, and the
  series adds no sparse warnings.

How this was made: an AI coding assistant (Claude, in Claude Code) wrote
the patches, the userspace replay and these messages at my direction;
I ran the hardware tests on my machines.

